From f094f22d1394c0633fea1eeb7f7b2bd87baba6c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:58:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] volumes: preserve immutable direct-volume mount plans

Container creation must use the same disk-to-mount plan that was
accepted when the PodVM was created. Parse each Pod direct-volume
directory once and retain an immutable normalized plan instead of
reparsing mutable host files for each container.

Validate the versioned metadata and preserve readonly, mount options,
fsGroup and CDH references. Reject duplicate disks and oversized plans,
and return independent option slices without expanding the public
provider interface.

Signed-off-by: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Generated-by: OpenAI Codex
